# Upstream clone of https://github.com/PepperSieve/Zombie (no license / all
# rights reserved). Retained locally for research/benchmarking only; never
# redistribute. Reproduce via scripts/download_zombie.py (pinned commit logged
# in docs/download_zombie.log).
zombie/

# Scraped Microsoft Purview SIT specs (proximity/pattern/keywords) pulled from
# learn.microsoft.com by scripts/retrieve_ms_dlp.py. Microsoft's curated
# compilation -- used as research facts only, not redistributed. Regenerate
# locally; provenance (source_url/etag/Last-Modified) is in each record and in
# docs/retrieve_record.log.
raw_data_records/

# Provenance logs the scripts above cite by name.  The repo-root `*.log`
# rule would otherwise drop them, leaving every provenance pointer in this
# pipeline dangling in the shipped artifact.
#
# download_zombie.log had two absolute toolchain paths under the packing
# account's home directory -- an IDENTITY_PATTERNS hit that would have made
# prepare.py's step_verify die().  Those two lines now read `~/.cargo/...`.
# The redaction is at source, not in the exporter, because CONTENT_FIXES
# only reaches files ending in ARCHIVE_SUFFIXES; step_scrub skips loose
# files.  Nothing is lost: the record is that cargo/rustc were FOUND, not
# where, and the load-bearing fact (the pinned upstream commit) is
# unaffected and is also restated in ../README.md.
!docs/retrieve_record.log
!docs/reg_pat_samples.log
!docs/download_zombie.log
